:: OC Kazu English Class Story [nobr]

/* Intro */
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alright everyone.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Mr. Hart</span> yawns as everyone takes their seats and gets ready for class. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Today we are going to be doing a writing exercise. Each of you will be writing a short story, at least two pages long, with yourselves as the main character. You can make the story about anything you want, as long as it’s school appropriate. Focus first on making it readable and coherent, as that is what you will be graded on. You can talk amongst yourselves, though the story must be completed by the end of class.”</span> He waves his hand for everyone to begin and sits at his desk to type away at his computer. <br>
<br>
Chatting begins instantly, with some talking about what sort of stories they are going to write while others consider doing crossovers with their friends. It is overall a creative atmosphere with only a few people goofing off. As you begin to ponder what you are going to write about, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">you notice <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span> going to town on his paper, writing like a machine with a smirk on his face.</span> Curious, you lean over and ask him what he’s writing about. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
	{
		Name: "OC Kazu",
		State: {
            Outfit: "Uniform",
			Mouth: "Smirk",
		},
	},
	{
		Name: "Player",
		State: {
			Mouth: "Frown",
		    },
	    },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sort of inspired by this book I like.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span> says, pausing at your surprised expression. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What? I like to read, as long as it’s good! You know, just because I’m cool, strong, and sexy, doesn’t mean I don’t have OTHER interests!”</span>  You chuckle, just saying it is a little surprising based on his personality. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span> scoffs at this, but you get him to perk back up by asking him about his story. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s about me and some friends being hunted down by a killer clown. Well, he looks like a clown but it actually an interdimensional creature of fear!”</span> <br>
<br>

<<if $OCKazuSocial > 40>>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I even put you in there!”</span> He smirks. <span style="Color: Pink">You smile at the idea that he considers you a friend but then get a bit nervous and ask what happens to you in the story.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, I couldn’t get TOO graphic, so I just had the monster eat your clothes and you spend the rest of the story in your tighty whities. Fitting, isn’t it?”</span> <span style="Color: LightGreen">You sigh at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span>’s teasing but feel good to at least be included.</span> <br>
    <br>
<</if>>

<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span> gets back to work, but he occasionally will chat about his ideas and check in on your own writing, offering writing advice that is actually pretty sound. <span style="Color: LightGreen">It is surprising that this is such a passion of his.</span> <br>
<<socialChange "Kazu" 3 1>>
<br>
<<include"Attend English Finish">>